==========================================================================================================
PART 4  VERDICTS  V1 line profile / V2 surface-brightness / V3 honest statement
==========================================================================================================

  V1  THE LINE PROFILE: a Gaussian in photon energy at E = m/2 = 2.5443 keV with sigma_E = E x sigma_v,los/c.  At the COMMITTED caustic/dust footing (G182 sigma_d = 140.2 km/s): sigma_E = 1.19 eV (FWHM 2.80 eV) -- the headline width.  The dark sector's own hotter footings widen it: the thermal width at T_dark = 334 K (Z7) is 6.05 eV (v_th = 713 km/s) and the core (beta-profile) width at sigma_r,core = 844 km/s (S04) is 7.16 eV (inner-bin sigma_los = 952 km/s caps the envelope at 8.08 eV).  THE FULL PREDICTED PROFILE: sigma_E in [1.19, 8.08] eV across the committed dark-sector velocity scales; the width is Doppler-dominated, never intrinsic (no rate predicted, A05).  HONEST READING: T_dark = m sigma_r^2/k_B by construction, so the thermal and kinematic widths are ONE velocity scale read two ways -- the committed 1.19 eV (cold dust/caustic) and the phantom's 6-7 eV are the two dark-sector faces of the same emitter.

  V2  THE SURFACE-BRIGHTNESS SIGNATURE: the line flux follows the dark density rho_ph = A/r^2 + A_d r^-1.7 inside r_M (G098 phantom + G139 dust class); with a constant rate the Abel projection gives I(b) = pi A_ph/b + 2 A_d K(0.7) b^-0.7 -- the phantom b^-1 CUSP (exact, numerically verified) plus the shallower dust b^-0.7 (numerically verified).  The composite local slope -d ln I/d ln b runs in [0.7, 1.0] inside r_M, steepening INWARD to the phantom cusp: at b = 0.1 r_M the composite sits 6.4x above its r_M level (the pure phantom 10x).  THE SEPARATION FROM CDM: an NFW halo projects FLAT-CORED (slope -> 0, 1.4x from 1 to 0.1 r_s) then steepens to -2; the framework's line DIVERGES toward the center where the CDM's is flat -- the innermost bins separate the composite from a CDM halo.

  V3  THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the three numbers that would confirm or kill the particle face: (1) THE ENERGY: E = m/2 = 2.5443 keV (band [2.50, 2.60]); a line at E != m/2 for the same m kills the m/2 relation (A05 kill band).  (2) THE WIDTH: sigma_E = 1.19 eV (envelope [1.19, 8.08] eV); a resolved width far outside E x sigma_v/c over the committed dark-sector velocity scales kills the kinematic reading.  (3) THE SPATIAL LAW: I(b) ~ b^-1 cusp (local slope -> 1 inward, in [0.7, 1.0] within r_M); a flat-cored (NFW-like) line surface brightness kills the phantom r^-2 face.  AND THE ENVIRONMENTAL SWITCH: the line is present in the frozen class (galaxy/group/cluster, z* >= 0) and absent in the never-froze dwarfs (dSph/UFD, z* < 0, G213) -- a 2.55-keV line from a UFD kills the freeze-map face independently of the rate.  The honest limits: the framework predicts the ENERGY, the WIDTH and the SPATIAL LAW, not the RATE -- non-observation everywhere kills only the radiative implementation, never the mass; the width is Doppler-dominated and the thermal/core footings are one velocity scale; the cusp-vs-core is a projected-density statement from the committed r^-2 phantom.

